margincode-bench: --agent-user benchagent: refusing to run.
As user benchagent (uid 1000) a session could:
  enter /m2b/bench-work/runs/fp2e5 (an earlier run's sessions)
  enter /m2b/bench-work/runs/fp3fe (an earlier run's sessions)
  enter /m2b/bench-work/ws/bfp2e5-relay-bus-resubscribe-av-1 (workspaces the daemon kept)
  enter /m2b/bench-work/ws/bfp2e5-relay-quote-split-av-1 (workspaces the daemon kept)
  enter /m2b/bench-work/ws/bfp2e5-relay-tax-with-rate-av-1 (workspaces the daemon kept)
  enter /m2b/bench-work/ws/bfp3fe-relay-bus-resubscribe-av-1 (workspaces the daemon kept)
  enter /m2b/bench-work/ws/bfp3fe-relay-quote-split-av-1 (workspaces the daemon kept)
  enter /m2b/bench-work/ws/bfp3fe-relay-tax-with-rate-av-1 (workspaces the daemon kept)
  enter /m2b/bench-work/ws/ddf2cd6-relay-bus-resubscribe (workspaces the daemon kept)
  enter /m2b/bench-work/ws/ddf3c-relay-bus-resubscribe (workspaces the daemon kept)
  enter /m2b/bench-work/ws/ddf3c-relay-quote-split (workspaces the daemon kept)
  enter /m2b/bench-work/ws/ddf3c-relay-tax-with-rate (workspaces the daemon kept)
  write to /home/benchagent (that user's home in the password database: what a session leaves there, a later one finds)
  list /home/benchagent (that user's home in the password database: what a session leaves there, a later one finds)
Close each of them to that user. For a directory only the harness needs, `chmod 700` on it (or on the top of a mounted bench tree) is enough: root still reads it. The daemon's workspace root needs `chmod 711`. The user's own home is closed by giving the user one that does not exist (`usermod -d /nonexistent benchagent`) or by making it root's alone (`chown root:root /home/benchagent && chmod 700 /home/benchagent`).
An earlier run's directory under /m2b/bench-work/runs is open to that user (a run keeps its own open only while it runs; one left open was left by a run that was killed or by an older harness). Once no run is using it, close it, or remove it if it is empty:
  chmod 700 /m2b/bench-work/runs/fp2e5
  chmod 700 /m2b/bench-work/runs/fp3fe
The harness does not do this itself: another run may be using it, and its sessions need to enter it.
